# WHAT THE PUBLIC SOURCE TARBALL DOES NOT CARRY (operator WORD 17 (d), landed as
# AMENDMENT 14 (d); WORD 24 RULING B). `build_dmg.sh` takes the tarball with
# `git archive`, which ships every tracked path, so the exclusion has to live
# here. These two directories are the fleet's own working surface, not the
# product's source:
#
#   reports/  — every desk's ledger, QUESTIONS-FOR-BILL, the wake payloads, the
#               audits and the rights sheets. 120 files as of today.
#   .claude/  — this machine's agent configuration and hooks. 88 files.
#
# The mirror provenance headers that name the frozen specification repository
# STAY (WORD 17 (d)); nothing here touches contracts/.
#
# Verify before a tarball is cut, never assume:
#   git check-attr export-ignore -- reports/INTEGRATION-log.md .claude/settings.json
#   (a trailing slash is NOT a directory pattern here as it is in .gitignore —
#    the directory itself and an explicit /** are both listed for that reason)
#   git archive HEAD | tar -t | grep -c '^reports/'      # expect 0
reports export-ignore
reports/** export-ignore
.claude export-ignore
.claude/** export-ignore
